# beta: the angle between the ABSORPTION transition dipole (at the S0 minimum)
# and the EMISSION transition dipole (at the relaxed S1 minimum).
#
# WHY THIS PARAMETER. The anisotropy and superradiance measurements are treated
# as constraining the same inter-chromophore angle, which makes them
# contradictory for ANY geometry (cos^2 x <= |cos x|, and the anisotropy needs
# <cos^2> = 0.436 while superradiance allows <|cos|> <= 0.287). But they do not
# measure the same angle: superradiance uses the angle between the two
# TRANSITION dipoles, while depolarisation compares the dipole that ABSORBED on
# one chromophore with the one that EMITTED on the other. If emission is rotated
# by beta from absorption within a chromophore, the anisotropy angle is a + beta
# and the inequality no longer binds a. beta ~ 20 deg reconciles the crystal /
# converged-MD geometry with both experiments; beta ~ 12 deg does it for the
# AlphaFold3 register.
#
# Same level as the vibronic parameters (CAM-B3LYP/6-31G*, charge -1) so beta is
# consistent with the S and omega already in use. Gas phase, 41-atom QM region
# plus 3 link H, exactly as the frequency chain.
coordinates s0_geom.xyz
run minimize
cis yes
cisnumstates 5
cistarget 1
cismaxiter 300
method camb3lyp
basis 6-31gs
charge -1
spinmult 1
scf diis+a
threall 1.0e-13
new_minimizer yes
nstep 300
gpus 1
end
